        "id": 2022258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-13T19:39:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "During a battery swap, it is crucial to ensure that the device remains in a suspended state, relying on a limited backup power source. It is essential to prevent any unintended awakenings in this state, as they could potentially lead to sudden surges in the power consumption, ultimately resulting in a device shutdown. Hence, we disable alarmtimer IRQs when in batteryswap mode.",
      "parentUuid": "1979d430_9ebc0645",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 258,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 258,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ef0f59c570e3c1168bcff2a6dcd6ace942655c89",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8460837a_9bb3b4d0",
        "filename": "kernel/time/alarmtimer.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 258,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-13T20:03:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the challenges we encounter is the occurrence of random RTC events that can cause unintended wake-ups during the battery swap. These events, happening unpredictably, disrupt the process and can lead to device shutdowns. Addressing and resolving these RTC events is essential to ensure a smooth battery swap experience and minimize any potential disruptions.",
      "parentUuid": "d4006db1_6250cdc0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 258,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 258,
